direction: right
title: Operating System Process vs. Thread Memory Model

OSProcess: OS Process (Dedicated Address Space) {
  style.fill: "#0B132B"
  style.stroke: "#1D4ED8"
  isolation: "Hardware MMU isolation; private virtual address space"
  ipc: "IPC required: Sockets, pipes, shared memory (serialization overhead)"
}

ThreadModel: Intra-Process Thread Model {
  style.fill: "#06201B"
  style.stroke: "#047857"
  
  Heap: Shared Process Heap & Metaspace {
    desc: "Shared directly by all threads; zero serialization"
  }
  
  T1: Thread 1 (Private Stack & PC)
  T2: Thread 2 (Private Stack & PC)
  
  T1 -> Heap: Direct pointer access
  T2 -> Heap: Concurrent memory contention
}

OSProcess -> ThreadModel: Process contains one or more threads
